# Local-only planning knowledge base
docs/

# Test-count reports (IMP-128). Written by `jest --json` and Playwright's json reporter in CI, read
# once by scripts/check-test-counts.mjs, and meaningless afterwards — they are a measurement of a
# particular run, not source. Committing one would also make the guard checkable against a stale
# file instead of a live suite.
test-count-*.json

# Playwright (IMP-094): traces, screenshots and the HTML report are per-run diagnostics, not source.
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# Claude Code local session state (scheduled task locks, local settings). Not tracked today; listed
# so it cannot be swept in by a `git add -A`. Anything in here that is genuinely meant to be shared
# should be moved out rather than un-ignored.
.claude/

# Throwaway Postgres clusters. `e2e/global-setup.js` and the API suite both boot one when
# DATABASE_URL is unset, and a data directory is ~66 MB of binary state that must never reach a
# commit. One did land in the repo root once — a helper script fell back to `$PWD` when its
# scratch-directory variable was unset — and it went unstaged only because Postgres creates the
# directory 0700 and git could not read it. That is luck, not a guard. This is the guard.
pgdata*/
